A||||8||sailordude||Has anyone used these?||||1||
Z||000000||sailordude||11-08-2001||07:37 PM||||Just wondering if anyone out there has put in the MSD Ignition or the ADS Super Chip in their cars.  If so how much did they cost you with installation, also what were the pros and cons of having them in.<P>Thanks again guys,<P>Darren||||reg||1
Z||000001||Boomtastic||11-08-2001||09:25 PM||||I've got an MSD 6AL in my Formula. It was necessary with the bored 2.8 and the additional fuel being dumped into it. I've been happy, especially with the programmable rev limiter. Doing burn outs without a care in the world about over-revving the motor is pure bliss!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> The ignition module should cost you around $200. Spring for the GM harness connector while you're at it and save yourself some wiring hassels.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||11-08-2001||10:41 PM||||I'd skip the chip- there are a lot of people here that say that the aftermarket chips are not enough of an improvement to justify the cost.<BR>I also have an MSD 6a and matching cannister Blaster coil. Go with the Blaster 3, the old looking can coils run cooler and have higher voltage than the stock style coil. <BR>I love the MSD on my car- I ran it for about 3 years on a 454 powered Suburban and then swapped it onto the Fiero when I added the 3.4 engine. While tuning chips, I was really off on the mixture and it would blow huge amounts of fuel smoke, but never fouled a plug.||||reg||1
Z||000003||filthyscarecrow||11-08-2001||11:32 PM||||i had a stock 85Gt adn now i have an 86SE with the ADS chip (it was my dad's car, he put it on). i think the 85Gt felt faster. i really don't think the chip does much. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||11-08-2001||11:35 PM||||I just have the MSD stock replacement... nothing fancy.  But I've had no problems with it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||11-09-2001||10:01 AM||||I'm planning on doing the MSD 6al igintion system (next year, maybe even this winter).  Also, I've got the ADS "Strip" chip.  I haven't installed it yet- I'm waiting for my G-Tech to arrive so I can run before and after tests (0-60, 1/4mi, rwhp) just to see if anything changes.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||sailordude||11-09-2001||12:35 PM||||So what you guys are saying is get the ignition but not the chip.<P>What about cool air induction? is that worth the money?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||11-09-2001||12:54 PM||||Sailor... you're just askin' for trouble  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Chips, as well as the Cold Air induction have been heated topics of debate here.  There was a statement- somewhere- on a webpage- by a "qualified" tech person stating that the Fiero was tested on a Dyno with the Stock intake, as well as with an "open" intake.  They found there to be little or no difference.  Many people argue about the fact that a stationary Dyno test does not influence a cold/ram air intake due to the absense of forced air from traveling speeds. You decided (I'd suggest searching through the tech & tech archive sections and reading whatever you can.<P>Most people say "Ignition- Definitely worth it" "Chip- Not worth it" "Cold Air- 50/50"||||reg||1
Z||000008||filthyscarecrow||11-09-2001||12:55 PM||||you already have cool air induction. look at the intake system. it's not gonna give you any hp, but it'll make it sound a bit different. mine hissed at idle when i took out the resonator adn water trap. i just replaced it with 3" aluminum ducting from home depot. total cost? $3.||||reg||1
